thermal/mineral weathering\"\n      },\n      \"mechanism\": \"Environmental provisioning and recycling of H\u2082S and Cu\u2070 over time via redox, volcanic, and geochemical cycling.\",\n      \"reasoning\": \"Supported by documented sources in Patel et al. (2015) and literature for surface delivery of both H\u2082S and native copper.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"rxn_008\",\n      \"name\": \"Alternative 3-aminopropanal supply from ammonia pool\",\n      \"inputs\": [\"mol_009\"],\n      \"outputs\": [\"mol_001\"],\n      \"environment\": \"Surface\",\n      \"agents\": [null],\n      \"conditions\": {\n        \"temperature\": \"320-340K\",\n        \"pressure\": \"ambient\",\n        \"catalyst\": null,\n        \"aqueous\": true,\n        \"other\": \"Speculative sequence (ammonia + carbonyl compounds, e.g. acrolein)\"\n      },\n      \"mechanism\": \"Reductive amination of C3 carbonyl species (e.g., acrolein) by NH\u2083, forming 3-aminopropanal.\",\n      \"reasoning\": \"Not directly demonstrated for this network; speculative but plausible based on cyanosulfidic primary amine chemistry cited in Patel et al. (2015), supporting a closed N-cycling network.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"rxn_009\",\n      \"name\": \"Alternative hydrolysis: pyrrolidine-2-carbonitrile \u2192 intermediate amide\",\n      \"inputs\": [\"mol_007\", \"mol_010\"],\n      \"outputs\": [\"mol_012\"],\n      \"environment\": \"Surface\",\n      \"agents\": [null],\n      \"conditions\": {\n        \"temperature\": \"300-320K\",\n        \"pressure\": \"ambient\",\n        \"catalyst\": null,\n        \"aqueous\": true,\n        \"other\": \"slow at neutral pH\"\n      },\n      \"mechanism\": \"Partial hydrolysis of the nitrile to the amide (pyrrolidine-2-carboxamide).\",\n      \"reasoning\": \"Mechanistically required one-protonation path (cited in Patel et al., 2015) but not isolated in that study; included here for pathway diversity.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"rxn_010