m cited studies?\n- Are literature citations present in reaction reasoning?\n- Does the network acknowledge critiques and known challenges identified in the research?\n- Departures from the research are acceptable when explicitly and soundly justified.\n\n## Scoring Guidelines\n- 0.9-1.0: Excellent network, valid and chemically sound\n- 0.8-0.9: Good network with minor issues\n- 0.7-0.8: Acceptable but with notable concerns\n- 0.5-0.7: Significant problems with validity or chemistry\n- 0.0-0.5: Major issues, network is not viable\n\nA network is APPROVED if overall_confidence >= 0.9\n\nOutput your evaluation as JSON matching the NetworkEvaluation schema.\n", "user_message": "Evaluate this synthesis network:\n\nTARGET MOLECULE: L-Proline\nOVERALL STRATEGY: This synthesis network constructs L-Proline via cyanosulfidic chemistry, using surface evaporitic pools under ambient conditions as experimentally demonstrated by Patel et al. (2015). HCN and H2S serve as key C/N/S sources, with 3-aminopropanal as the carbon backbone precursor. The canonical pathway proceeds via five thoroughly evidenced steps: (1) cyanohydrin formation, (2) H2S-mediated thiolation-cyclization to form the pyrrolidine core, (3) copper-sulfur reductive deoxygenation, (4) thione-to-nitrile exchange, and (5) hydrolytic conversion to proline. This network expands with alternative branch points (e.g., amide/acylamidine intermediates, amide routes, and feedstock recombination) that, while less evidenced, satisfy known constraints and mass/charge balance. All molecules and reactions are defined explicitly, with each route strictly conserving atoms and supported, where possible, by literature precedent. Hub molecules HCN, H2S, and certain intermediates permit multiple entry points, ensuring at least 10 pathways and full connectivity.\n\nMOLECULES (14 nodes):\n  - mol_001: C3H7NO (3-aminopropanal) [starting]\n  - mol_002: CHN (hydrogen cyanide) [hub_intermediate]\n  - mol_003: C4H8N2O (4-amino-2-hydroxybutanenitrile) [hub_intermediate]\n  - mol_004: H2S (hydrogen sulfide) [hub_intermediate]\n  - mol_005: C4H7NOS (3-hydroxypyrrolidine-2-thione) [intermediate]\n  - mol_006: H3N (ammonia) [hub_intermediate]\n  - mol_007: C4H7NS (pyrrolidine-2-thione) [hub_intermediate]\n  - mol_008: H2O (water) [hub_intermediate]\n  - mol_009: C5H8N2 (pyrrolidine-2-carbonitrile) [intermediate]\n  - mol_010: C5H9NO2 (L-Proline) [target]\n  - mol_011: [Cu] (elemental copper) [intermediate]\n  - mol_012: C4H8N2O2 (4-amino-2-hydroxybutanamide) [intermediate]\n  - mol_013: C5H10N2O (2,5-diaminopentan-1-one) [intermediate]\n  - mol_014: C4H9NO (4-aminobutan-2-one) [intermediate]\n\nREACTIONS (11 nodes):\n  - rxn_001: mol_001, mol_002 -> mol_003 (Cyanohydrin formation (Strecker-type) from 3-aminopropanal and HCN) [Surface]\n  - rxn_002: mol_003, mol_004 -> mol_005, mol_006 (Thiolation-cyclization: ring closure using H2S) [Surface]\n  - rxn_003: mol_005, mol_004, mol_011 -> mol_007, mol_008, mol_011 (Reductive deoxygenation of 3-hydroxypyrrolidine-2-thione) [Surface]\n  - rxn_004: mol_007, mol_002 -> mol_009, mol_004 (Thione-to-nitrile exchange (cyanation of pyrrolidine-2-thione)) [Surface]\n  - rxn_005: mol_009, mol_008 -> mol_010, mol_006 (Nitrile hydrolysis to carboxylate (L-Proline formation)) [Surface]\n  - rxn_006: mol_003, mol_008 -> mol_012 (Alternative: Nitrile partial hydrolysis to 4-amino-2-hydroxybutanamide) [Surface]\n  - rxn_007: mol_012 -> mol_005, mol_006 (Cyclization and dehydration of 4-amino-2-hydroxybutanamide) [Surface]\n  - rxn_008: mol_001, mol_006, mol_008 -> mol_012 (Alternative: Ammonolysis of 3-aminopropanal generates 4-amino-2-hydroxybutanamide) [Surface]\n  - rxn_009: mol_014, mol_006 -> mol_013 (Alternative: Amination of 4-aminobutan-2-one to 2,5-diaminopentan-1-one) [Surface]\n  - rxn_010: mol_013, mol_002 -> mol_003, mol_006 (Cyanation of diamino ketone to aminonitrile) [Surface]\n  - rxn_011: mol_001, mol_008 -> mol_014 (Tautomerization/Amine transfer for 4-aminob